<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>What Is It All About?</title>
    <style>

        :root {
            --night: #071a33;
            --deep-blue: #0b2f5b;
            --blue: #124f8c;
            --sky: #dbeeff;
            --ice: #f5fbff;
            --gold: #f3c96b;
            --white: #ffffff;
            --ink: #17314f;
            --shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 16, 43, 0.28);
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        html {
            scroll-behavior: smooth;
        }

        body {
            margin: 0;
            min-height: 100vh;
            color: var(--white);
            background:
                radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(87, 166, 235, 0.35), transparent 34rem),
                radial-gradient(circle at bottom right, rgba(243, 201, 107, 0.12), transparent 28rem),
                linear-gradient(145deg, var(--night), var(--deep-blue) 48%, var(--blue));
            font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
            line-height: 1.75;
        }

        .page-shell {
            width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 32px));
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 48px 0 64px;
        }

        .hero {
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden;
            padding: 62px 54px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);
            border-radius: 34px;
            background:
                linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)),
                rgba(4, 27, 57, 0.66);
            box-shadow: var(--shadow);
            backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
        }

        .hero::after {
            content: "";
            position: absolute;
            right: -90px;
            top: -90px;
            width: 270px;
            height: 270px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(243, 201, 107, 0.35);
            border-radius: 50%;
            box-shadow:
                0 0 0 34px rgba(243, 201, 107, 0.06),
                0 0 0 68px rgba(243, 201, 107, 0.04);
        }

        .eyebrow {
            margin: 0 0 12px;
            color: var(--gold);
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 0.18em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        h1 {
            max-width: 760px;
            margin: 0;
            font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5.4rem);
            line-height: 0.98;
            letter-spacing: -0.035em;
        }

        .hero-subtitle {
            max-width: 760px;
            margin: 28px 0 0;
            color: #d7ebff;
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.22rem);
            line-height: 1.65;
        }

        .content-grid {
            display: grid;
            gap: 28px;
            margin-top: 30px;
        }

        .card {
            padding: clamp(28px, 5vw, 50px);
            border-radius: 28px;
            color: var(--ink);
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--white), var(--ice));
            box-shadow: var(--shadow);
        }

        .card.blue-card {
            color: var(--white);
            background:
                linear-gradient(140deg, rgba(18, 79, 140, 0.96), rgba(8, 43, 82, 0.98));
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.13);
        }

        .section-label {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-bottom: 18px;
            padding: 7px 12px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            color: var(--deep-blue);
            background: var(--sky);
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.72rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            letter-spacing: 0.1em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .blue-card .section-label {
            color: #09294f;
            background: var(--gold);
        }

        h2 {
            margin: 0 0 22px;
            color: inherit;
            font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3.5vw, 2.6rem);
            line-height: 1.15;
        }

        p {
            margin: 0 0 1.15em;
            font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.22rem);
        }

        p:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        .short-line {
            margin: 0.28em 0;
            font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.42rem);
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 0.01em;
        }

        .quote-box {
            position: relative;
            margin: 34px 0;
            padding: 34px 34px 34px 42px;
            border-left: 6px solid var(--gold);
            border-radius: 18px;
            color: var(--white);
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0b2f5b, #155e9e);
            box-shadow: 0 16px 34px rgba(0, 37, 78, 0.22);
        }

        .quote-box::before {
            content: "“";
            position: absolute;
            left: 16px;
            top: -14px;
            color: rgba(243, 201, 107, 0.42);
            font-size: 5rem;
            line-height: 1;
        }

        .quote-box p {
            position: relative;
            margin: 0;
            font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 2.05rem);
            font-style: italic;
            line-height: 1.35;
        }

        .quote-stack {
            display: grid;
            gap: 16px;
            margin: 34px 0;
        }

        .quote-stack .quote-box {
            margin: 0;
        }

        .closing-card {
            text-align: center;
        }

        .home-link {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 34px;
            padding: 14px 22px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28);
            border-radius: 999px;
            color: var(--white);
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration: none;
            transition: transform 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
        }

        .home-link:hover,
        .home-link:focus {
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.17);
        }

        .footer-note {
            margin-top: 18px;
            color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65);
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.86rem;
        }

        @media (max-width: 700px) {
            .page-shell {
                width: min(100% - 20px, 1120px);
                padding-top: 20px;
            }

            .hero {
                padding: 42px 26px;
                border-radius: 24px;
            }

            .card {
                border-radius: 22px;
            }

            .quote-box {
                padding: 28px 24px 28px 34px;
            }
        }

    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main class="page-shell">
        <header class="hero">
            <p class="eyebrow">Zion Coalition · My Jesus-Greg WORLD</p>
            <h1>What Is It All About?</h1>
            <p class="hero-subtitle">A reflection on sense-making, the recurring questions of discipleship, and the larger patterns that slowly come into view.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="content-grid">
            <article class="card blue-card">
                <span class="section-label">The Recurring Question</span>
                <p>For more than a decade, as Jesus and I have built what I call <em>My Jesus-Greg WORLD</em>, a recurring pattern has emerged.</p>
                <p>Every week—or at least it often seems that way—I find myself stepping back from whatever I have been building. It is as though Jesus gently interrupts my thoughts and asks a question from thirty thousand feet above the landscape.</p>
                <div class="quote-stack">
                    <blockquote class="quote-box">
                        <p>What is this all about?</p>
                    </blockquote>
                    <blockquote class="quote-box">
                        <p>Why are you doing this?</p>
                    </blockquote>
                </div>
                <p>The question rarely feels like a request for information. It feels more like an invitation.</p>
                <p class="short-line">An invitation to see more.</p>
                <p class="short-line">An invitation to climb higher.</p>
                <p>An invitation to discover that all of the individual projects, essays, symbols, songs, routines, experiments, and conversations belong to something larger than I had previously understood.</p>
                <p>Over the years I have come to recognize this as one of the recurring rhythms of my discipleship.</p>
                <p class="short-line">The answer is never final.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Instead, the question returns.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Again.</p>
                <p class="short-line">And again.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Each time I answer it from a slightly higher mountain.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <span class="section-label">Reflection 2</span>
                <h2>The Human Work of Meaning</h2>
                <p class="short-line">Human beings seem naturally wired for this process.</p>
                <p>We do not simply gather facts. We organize them into meaning.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Scientists do this.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Authors do this.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Filmmakers do this.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Teachers do this.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Parents do this.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Civilizations do this.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Every field eventually arrives at the same question.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Physics explains electrons.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Biology explains living cells.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Psychology explains minds.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Sociology explains societies.</p>
                <blockquote class="quote-box">
                    <p>What is it all about?</p>
                </blockquote>
                <p>The deepest discoveries often come not from collecting one more fact, but from discovering a larger pattern that allows thousands of facts to fit together.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Meaning emerges.</p>
                <p class="short-line">The picture becomes clearer.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <span class="section-label">Reflection 3</span>
                <h2>Names for the Pattern</h2>
                <p class="short-line">Philosophers have given names to this process.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Some call it <em>sense-making.</em></p>
                <p>Others speak of <em>hermeneutics</em>—the continual interpretation of meaning.</p>
                <p>Psychologists describe <em>narrative identity</em>, our lifelong effort to understand the story we are living.</p>
                <p>Still others describe a <em>hermeneutic spiral</em>: we revisit the same questions repeatedly, but because we ourselves have changed, every return reveals something new.</p>
                <p class="short-line">It is not a circle.</p>
                <p class="short-line">It is a spiral.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Each revolution carries us a little higher.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card blue-card">
                <span class="section-label">Reflection 4</span>
                <h2>The Question Returns</h2>
                <p class="short-line">That is how this project has unfolded for me.</p>
                <p>Many times I have believed I finally understood what Jesus was building.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Then the question returns.</p>
                <blockquote class="quote-box">
                    <p>What is it all about?</p>
                </blockquote>
                <p class="short-line">The previous answer is rarely discarded.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Instead, it becomes one piece of a larger answer.</p>
                <p>Like climbing a mountain, every new overlook allows me to see why the previous overlook mattered.</p>
                <p class="short-line">It was not wrong.</p>
                <p class="short-line">It simply was not high enough.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <span class="section-label">Reflection 5</span>
                <h2>A Different Game</h2>
                <p>One of the most recent answers to that recurring question has become especially important.</p>
                <p>Jesus has been inviting me to understand discipleship itself as learning to play an entirely different game.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Not a game in the sense of pretending.</p>
                <p>A game in the sense of entering a world with a new scoreboard.</p>
                <p class="short-line">New rules.</p>
                <p class="short-line">New objectives.</p>
                <p class="short-line">New victories.</p>
                <p class="short-line">New ways of measuring success.</p>
                <p>The Scriptures are filled with moments when God invited people to stop keeping score according to the world's rules and begin seeing reality according to heaven's.</p>
                <p>That insight eventually became the foundation of another essay.</p>
                <p>For now, it stands at the entrance to <em>My Jesus-Greg WORLD</em> because it has become one of the clearest answers I have yet received to Jesus' recurring question:</p>
                <blockquote class="quote-box">
                    <p>What is it all about?</p>
                </blockquote>
                <p class="short-line">At least for now.</p>
                <p class="short-line">Until He asks me again.</p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <div class="closing-card">
            <a class="home-link" href="index.html">Return to Home</a>
            <p class="footer-note">Zion Coalition</p>
        </div>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
